[state-contract] State-aware interaction contract (complete)
Files: proposals/input-and-interaction.md
Do: Reconcile the input contract to one concrete rule: interaction logic receives a read-only selected Caravan GameState together with SemanticInputBatch and Tau. InputPacketSet remains only a derived membership compatibility view. The state is the result of querying the selected immutable worldline at the selected LogicalTime, and carries that exact logical time itself. Keep Frame, Renderer, DrawCommand, backend state, host time, and journal mutation outside the seam. Record error and ownership expectations without introducing a second authoritative state model or an alternative candidate contract.
Accept: The proposal names the exact state-aware interaction boundary, says that Tau does not select logical state, says that input queries never inspect rendered output, and agrees with the current immutable worldline and journal-only publication rules. If the target wording is already present, the task is complete without churn.
> Decision: The interaction seam is state-aware; it does not receive rendered output.
